    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 360\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 7770, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the Indian law, in relation to the state recogni-\n      tion and acknowledgment of the Montaukett Indians\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would establish state recognition of the Montaukett  Indians\nand  further set out eligibility of members of the Nation to vote in its\nelections, the terms of office for the elected officials of the  Nation,\nand the process by which elections shall take place.\n \n  I  have  previously  vetoed  two  similar  bills attempting to provide\nrecognition of a group through the use of legislation. In 2013, I issued\nVeto No. 210 in which I noted that the State did not have an administra-\ntive procedure to determine how a group could receive State recognition.\nIn that veto message, I directed the Department of  State  to  establish\nsuch  a  procedure, which they have done. In 2017, I issued Veto No. 174\nin which I noted that the legislation was premature. The  Department  of\nState  had  developed  a  procedure  and  the groups had begun to submit\npaperwork in response to that procedure.\n \n  As of the writing of this message, the Department of  State  is  still\nreceiving  supporting  documentation from the interested groups.  There-\nfore, just like in 2017, this legislation is  premature  and  we  should\nallow  the  administrative  process  to  take  its due course. Since the\nDepartment of State is still in the process of receiving  and  reviewing\nthe relevant documents, I cannot support this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
